<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_ScatterShrinesRare.xml             UtinniPatches - new file 2026-09-10
  ============================================================================
  MECH_PRESENCE_ENFORCEMENT_1, piece 2/4 support file. The ratified ANCIENT
  column (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/mechanoid_biome_presence_draft.md) marks
  four biomes RARE rather than ALLOW/DENY: ExtremeDesert, BiomeGRimond,
  PoisonForest, BiomeCypreJungle. The MECHANISM section's own recipe for a
  RARE ancient-danger biome: "prevent the stock genstep and add a cloned
  GenStepDef with a lower countPer10kCellsRange via extraGenSteps." This is
  that clone; AncientDangerGenSteps_AmbientDoctrine.xml is what wires it onto
  the four biomes (alongside preventGenSteps->ScatterShrines to stop the
  stock, full-rate version).

  EVERY FIELD BELOW IS COPIED FROM THE SHIPPED DONOR
  C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data\Core\Defs\MapGeneration\BasePlayerMapGenerator.xml:18-25
    <GenStepDef>
      <defName>ScatterShrines</defName>
      <order>750</order>
      <genStep Class="GenStep_ScatterShrines">
        <allowInWaterBiome>false</allowInWaterBiome>
        <countPer10kCellsRange><min>0.12</min><max>0.25</max></countPer10kCellsRange>
      </genStep>
    </GenStepDef>
  order and genStep Class are unchanged; allowInWaterBiome is unchanged (none
  of the four RARE biomes are water biomes anyway). The one deliberate change
  is countPer10kCellsRange, quartered from 0.12-0.25 to 0.03-0.0625 -
  "present but tuned sparse" per the table's own legend, and a concrete
  number this item has to pick since the spec names no ratio. Documented here
  rather than guessed silently; noted on MECH_PRESENCE_ENFORCEMENT_1 for the
  owner's awareness. True per-incident-worker tuning (matching AMBIENT's own
  RARE rows) would need C#/Harmony and is out of this item's XML-only scope.

  GenStepDef.cs / GenStep_ScatterShrines.cs read via rimsage confirm nothing
  else about this class is order- or biome-sensitive beyond these two fields;
  the class inherits GenStep_ScatterRuinsSimple's shrine-placement logic
  unchanged (guardian/pod content is resolved elsewhere - see the
  AncientDangerGenSteps_AmbientDoctrine.xml note on why shrine CONTENT
  curation, piece 4, could not be built in XML).
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef>
    <defName>RUT_ScatterShrinesRare</defName>
    <order>750</order>
    <genStep Class="GenStep_ScatterShrines">
      <allowInWaterBiome>false</allowInWaterBiome>
      <countPer10kCellsRange><min>0.03</min><max>0.0625</max></countPer10kCellsRange>
    </genStep>
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
